- op: discuss  # 5200
  at: '2026-04-07T02:03:24Z'  # 5200
  by: agent  # 5200
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5200
  clock: 3  # 5200
  nonce: '5200'  # 5200
  message: "Per user pushback (2026-04-06): unclear whether library_patterns is supposed to be wired into the annotator, or whether it was always meant for linker consumption like event_sourcing/message_queue. The Go go.yaml comment ('Name-based heuristics in library_patterns fill this gap') and the patterns themselves (method-name regexes with access_mode but no channel/edge_type) suggest they want to annotate generic call edges. ADR-0015 §3/§7 suggest library_patterns is for linker pattern-matching that produces specialized edge types (not annotation of generic calls edges). Three options for resolution: (a) delete unused Go library_patterns, (b) extend annotate_dataflow to apply library_patterns as per-language fallback, (c) leave alone and find a different remedy for the prometheus LOW_DATAFLOW_SLICE_RATIO WARN. Awaiting user direction."  # 5200
